  clock: 4  # 50ef
  nonce: 50ef  # 50ef
  message: "Done in PR #2251. Evidence against the close condition:\n(1) THE TEST. packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_selection_child_processes.py runs real coverage and the real fold of a recorder record into one index. test_a_test_that_starts_python_is_not_dropped_and_one_that_starts_gitleaks_is: four measured tests, none with a row on the changed function; the files of the one that starts python and of the one that runs git in a scratch repository are not droppable, the files of the plain one and of the one that starts only gitleaks are. The same at statement level in test_statement_select.py (a test that starts python and reached the changed function is selected whole and is not among the tests that could have been left out; one that starts only gitleaks is narrowed as before).\n(2) THE COUNTS, from the index after a full run of the branch (2026-11-18; 41,284 passed, 12 skipped, 30 xfailed in 688.58 s). The fold printed: never narrowed, besides the unmeasured: 412 test(s) start a program that can run Python (git-elsewhere 242, python 159, git 24); 4 test(s) have no read record. The 4 are ids of two deleted test files. At file level: 939 test files were droppable-capable by the old rule, 918 now: 21 files newly never dropped, 69.7 of 3,229 test-seconds; 15 of the 21 are held only because of git in a scratch repository. (The item's sizing of 192 mixed tests predates recording git run outside the repository.)\n(3) LIVE CONTROL on the test_import_closure.py case: import_closure.ImportGraph.__init__, the call that fills the importer map replaced by pass. 47 tests of the file fail. The by-statement selector asked about that fault alone: 43 selected; 4 not selected, all 4 named in Selection.cannot_speak (the two campaign cases, measured, recorded starting git and python, with no row on the function; and two unmeasured tests); 0 neither. File: fast_smart_test_build_11172026/childrule/live_control.txt.\n(4) MUTATIONS. 38 planted over this change and the spelling fix; 35 red at first. The three survivors: a check in without_xdist_group that could not fire (removed), and two test gaps (closed). All 38 red at the merged head. File: childrule/mutations.tsv.\nBEYOND THE ITEM'S TEXT: (a) the recorder used to leave nothing for a git run outside the repository; it runs hooks there, so it is now recorded as git-elsewhere, held by this rule and inert for the prose-only rule; recorder version 3. (b) a test in an xdist group was stored under two spellings (258 ids in 6 files), which broke the join to the read record; every way into the stores now drops the group suffix. (c) rustup is not in the cannot-run-Python list (rustup run executes a command); 1 test.\nNOT COVERED: exemptions rest on a program's name. An index id of a removed test in a file that has no record at all is still counted as having no read record (42 ids, all of deleted files). select_tests (selection by function) is unchanged: it goes on naming a test that has a row.\n"  # 50ef
